     carve (after each runner: #components / measure): k1:1c/0.715  k2:2c/0.572  k3:4c/0.381  k4:4c/0.238  k5:2c/0.058  k6:2c/0.017
     shrink ratios: [0.8, 0.667, 0.625, 0.242, 0.287]   (S527 predicts ~ (n-2)/n = 0.714)

  Each runner SPLITS the surviving feasible arc into sub-arcs: the carve
  tree mirrors the recursive sub-polygon tree of part A. The observer's
  apex (largest surviving arc) is a NESTED sequence of sub-apexes; LRC =
  'the recursive carving never empties the apex' (AP = tight: empties to 0).
